      "id": 1,
      "text": "Union Mills got its name from a gristmill built in the 1830s by Sylvanus Everts on Mill Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Union_Mills%2C_Indiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Joseph Wheaton laid out a small village at Mill Creek in 1832, and by 1838 only five log houses stood.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Union_Mills%2C_Indiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town was officially platted in 1849, though settlers had been there for years before.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Union_Mills%2C_Indiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Three railroad lines passing near Union Mills spurred growth in the late 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
